          "distinct": true,
          "id": "91b2ae1cad4d5209dbfe6236d3dc0ff353e161b0",
          "message": "docs(pluginsdk): Add thread safety, rate limiting, CORS, and perf docs (#243)\n\n- Add comprehensive documentation for production deployment patterns\n  covering thread safety guarantees, rate limiting strategies, CORS\n  configuration scenarios, and performance tuning guidelines\n- Create godoc examples demonstrating HTTP client ownership, concurrent\n  usage, high-throughput configuration, and FOCUS record building\n- Fix inline comments for contractedCostTolerance (IEEE 754 rationale),\n  WithTags copy semantics, and correlation pattern field reference\n- Update Table of Contents with new sections for discoverability\n\n- [x] All SDK tests pass (`go test ./sdk/go/...`)\n- [x] Go linting passes with zero issues (`golangci-lint run`)\n- [x] Markdown linting passes (`npm run lint:markdown`)\n- [x] Proto regeneration successful after correlation pattern fix\n- [x] Example functions compile and ExampleResourceMatcher validates\n\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/example_test.go` - Godoc examples for Client.Close(),\n  concurrent usage, HighThroughputClientConfig, FocusRecordBuilder, and\n  ResourceMatcher patterns\n\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/README.md` - Added Thread Safety, Rate Limiting,\n  Performance Tuning, and CORS Configuration sections with code examples\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/client.go` - Added HTTP client ownership semantics\n  documentation to NewClient() godoc\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/focus_conformance.go` - Expanded contractedCostTolerance\n  comment with IEEE 754 floating-point rationale and FOCUS 1.2 reference\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/focus_builder.go` - Added copy semantics and thread\n  safety documentation to WithTags() method\n- `proto/pulumicost/v1/costsource.proto` - Fixed correlation pattern\n  comment to reference ResourceRecommendationInfo.id (not resource_id)\n\nCloses #206\nCloses #207\nCloses #211\nCloses #231\nCloses #233\nCloses #235\nCloses #236\nCloses #237\nCloses #238\nCloses #240",
          "timestamp": "2025-12-31T10:22:40-06:00",
