          "distinct": true,
          "id": "4ba1da43a642939f1bceb42c8bf2ebd14b7d327d",
          "message": "feat(proto): add growth_type to projected cost response (#250)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Enables plugins to report growth hints to Core for smarter forecasting\n- Plugins can now indicate whether a resource is consumption-based (EC2,\n  Lambda) or accumulation-based (S3, backups) without Core needing\n  hardcoded resource-type knowledge\n- Aligns with existing GrowthType enum already used in\n  GetProjectedCostRequest and ResourceDescriptor\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make generate` regenerates protobuf code successfully\n- [x] `make test` passes with all tests\n- [x] `make lint` passes with zero issues (golangci-lint, buf, markdown, yaml)\n- [x] Generated Go code includes new `GrowthType` field and accessor method\n\n## Changes\n\n### Modified files\n\n- `proto/pulumicost/v1/costsource.proto` - Added `growth_type` field (field 6)\n  to `GetProjectedCostResponse` with documentation for usage patterns\n- `sdk/go/proto/pulumicost/v1/costsource.pb.go` - Regenerated with new field\n\nCloses #249",
          "timestamp": "2025-12-31T20:42:36-06:00",
          "tree_id": "4cc9a320fc35a520e832dade2188887404f19b53",
