          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6ed0a717debc4b64d545133a0e155c855c51f4cd",
          "message": "docs: add pulumicost to finfocus migration guide (#286)\n\nAdded complete migration documentation supporting the PulumiCost to FinFocus\nrename, including a user-facing guide and structured specification artifacts.\n\nThe migration guide covers environment variable updates, plugin discovery path\nchanges, and step-by-step migration instructions. Machine-readable migration\nmetadata in JSON format supports automation and tooling for plugin ecosystems.\n\nSpecification documents define migration scope, requirements, and implementation\ntasks. This enables both manual migration paths for operators and automated\ntooling support for plugin maintainers.\n\n- `MIGRATION.md` - User-facing migration guide with environment variable mappings\n  and step-by-step instructions for existing deployments\n- `llm-migration.json` - Machine-readable migration metadata and configuration\n- `specs/001-migration-docs/spec.md` - Detailed migration specification\n- `specs/001-migration-docs/plan.md` - Implementation and rollout plan\n- `specs/001-migration-docs/tasks.md` - Structured task breakdown\n- `specs/001-migration-docs/data-model.md` - Migration data structures\n- `specs/001-migration-docs/contracts` - Migration scope and boundaries\n- `specs/001-migration-docs/checklists/requirements.md` - Requirements checklist\n\n- [x] `make lint` passes with zero issues\n- [x] Markdown linting validates all migration documentation\n- [x] JSON schema validation for llm-migration.json\n- [x] Files follow project conventions and formatting standards\n\nCloses #282",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-13T06:47:16-06:00",
          "tree_id": "63efb25bc71700d0a7211d79992045594e9b0e36",
