          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8b5b97d903ccd1e1f95e975a41e34b2340e7341f",
          "message": "feat(sdk): implement github issues audit plan for #247-340 (#341)\n\n* feat(pricing): add validation bypass metadata for audit trails\n\n- Enables ValidationResult to carry metadata about bypassed validations\n  (e.g., when --yolo flag is used), providing audit trails that survive\n  stateless service boundaries via JSON serialization\n- Implements zero-allocation enum validation pattern (<10 ns/op) following\n  the established registry package optimization approach\n- Provides CLI display formatters and filter functions for compliance\n  reporting and historical analysis of bypass events\n\n- [x] `make test` passes - all unit and conformance tests pass\n- [x] `make lint` passes - 2 minor testpackage style warnings consistent\n      with existing codebase patterns\n- [x] Benchmarks verify <10 ns/op, 0 allocs/op performance targets\n- [x] Quickstart.md examples compile and execute correctly\n- [x] JSON round-trip serialization preserves all fields\n\n- `sdk/go/pricing/bypass.go` - BypassSeverity/BypassMechanism enums,\n  BypassMetadata struct, constructor with functional options, validation,\n  CLI formatters, and filter functions\n- `sdk/go/pricing/bypass_test.go` - Comprehensive test suite with enum\n  validation, constructor, truncation, JSON round-trip, and benchmark tests\n- `sdk/go/testing/bypass_conformance_test.go` - Conformance tests for JSON\n  compliance, cross-service boundary serialization, and backward compatibility\n\n- `sdk/go/pricing/observability.go` - Added Bypasses field to ValidationResult\n- `sdk/go/pricing/CLAUDE.md` - Added bypass metadata documentation\n- `specs/034-validation-bypass-metadata/tasks.md` - Marked all 45 tasks complete\n\nCloses #216\n\n* docs: Add docstrings to `034-validation-bypass-metadata` (#339)\n\nDocstrings generation was requested by @rshade.\n\n* https://github.com/rshade/finfocus-spec/pull/338#issuecomment-3795622941\n\nThe following files were modified:\n\n* `sdk/go/pricing/bypass.go`\n\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(sdk): implement github issues audit plan for #247-340\n\nThis PR completes the comprehensive audit of GitHub issues #247-340,\nclosing 9 already-implemented issues and implementing 5 new features:\n\n- **semver validation**: Added `Validate()` function with detailed error\n  messages for empty, missing prefix, and format violations\n- **context cancellation**: SerializeStream/Slice/Batch now support\n  graceful cancellation via context.Context\n- **prediction intervals**: GetProjectedCostResponse gains lower/upper\n  bounds and confidence level fields for forecasting uncertainty\n- **test coverage**: Added unexpired deadline test and validateCostValues\n  benchmarks (45-52 ns/op, 0 allocs)\n\n- [x] `make test` passes - all Go tests succeed\n- [x] `make lint` passes - Go, buf, markdown, YAML linting\n- [x] Prediction interval tests cover NaN/Inf panics, bounds validation\n- [x] Context cancellation tests verify timeout and cancel behavior\n- [x] Benchmark tests verify zero-allocation performance\n\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/focus_conformance_benchmark_test.go` - Benchmarks for\n  validateCostValues with NaN/Inf detection paths\n\n- `proto/finfocus/v1/costsource.proto` - Added prediction_interval_lower,\n  prediction_interval_upper, confidence_level fields\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers.go` - Added WithPredictionInterval option\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers_test.go` - Added prediction interval tests\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/context_test.go` - Added unexpired deadline tests\n- `sdk/go/jsonld/streaming.go` - Added context.Context to stream methods\n- `sdk/go/jsonld/streaming_test.go` - Added cancellation tests\n- `sdk/go/internal/semver/semver.go` - Added Validate() function\n- `sdk/go/internal/semver/semver_test.go` - Added validation tests\n\n- Removed leftover review_summary.md file\n- Fixed golines/goimports formatting in streaming.go\n\nCloses #247\nCloses #255\nCloses #264\nCloses #265\nCloses #314\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
