          "distinct": true,
          "id": "571a0cdd7c4a822e74dd4a688972bab35fa9afa7",
          "message": "feat(proto): add pagination support to actual cost retrieval (#360)\n\n* feat(currency): add symbol support and amount formatting (#357)\n\nAdds currency symbol support to the existing `sdk/go/currency/` package,\nenabling plugins to display monetary amounts with proper symbols, decimal\nprecision based on ISO 4217 MinorUnits, and thousands separators. This\neliminates duplicated symbol lookup code across FinFocus plugins.\n\n- [x] All existing currency tests pass\n- [x] New symbol tests pass (GetSymbol, FormatAmount, FormatAmountNoSymbol)\n- [x] Benchmarks meet targets (GetSymbol <55 ns/op, 0 allocs)\n- [x] `make lint` passes with zero issues\n- [x] `make test` passes\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/symbol.go` - GetSymbol(), FormatAmount(),\n  FormatAmountNoSymbol() helper functions with thousands separator support\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/symbol_test.go` - Comprehensive tests for symbol lookup\n  and amount formatting edge cases\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/currency.go` - Added Symbol field to Currency struct,\n  updated all 180 currency entries with symbols (empty for currencies\n  without commonly used symbols like CHF, XAU, XDR)\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/currency_test.go` - Added TestCurrency_Symbol and\n  TestGetCurrency_SymbolCopy tests\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/benchmark_test.go` - Added BenchmarkGetSymbol,\n  BenchmarkFormatAmount, and BenchmarkFormatAmountNoSymbol\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/doc.go` - Updated package documentation with symbol\n  and formatting examples\n\n- `sdk/go/currency/CLAUDE.md` - Updated with new functions and patterns\n\n- `sdk/go/CLAUDE.md` - Updated currency package description and usage\n  examples\n\n* feat(proto): add pagination support to actual cost retrieval\n\n- Enables hosts to retrieve large cost datasets (10,000+ records)\n  in manageable pages via offset-based pagination tokens\n- Adds `page_size`/`page_token` request fields and\n  `next_page_token`/`total_count` response fields to the proto\n- Provides server-side `PaginateActualCosts()` helper in Go SDK\n  and client-side `ActualCostIterator` for transparent page\n  iteration in both Go and TypeScript\n- Maintains full backward compatibility: existing plugins and hosts\n  work unchanged when pagination fields are absent\n- Includes 8 conformance tests validating distinct pagination\n  behaviors and performance benchmarks (<100ms p99 per page)\n\n- [x] `make test` passes (all Go packages)\n- [x] `golangci-lint run ./...` passes with 0 issues\n- [x] TypeScript client build passes (`tsup` + `tsc --noEmit`)\n- [x] TypeScript tests pass (56/56 including 5 pagination tests)\n- [x] `BenchmarkPaginateActualCosts`: 112 ns/op, 2 allocs/op\n- [x] `BenchmarkGetActualCostPaginated/FullIteration`: ~5ms for\n  10K records (SC-002 target: <10s)\n- [x] 8 pagination conformance tests pass\n- [x] Backward compatibility tests pass (legacy plugin/host)\n- [x] All 51 implementation tasks verified complete\n\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/actual_cost_iterator.go` - Go client-side\n  page iterator for `GetActualCost` responses\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/actual_cost_iterator_test.go` - Iterator\n  unit tests (multi-page, single-page, error, empty, context)\n- `sdk/go/testing/pagination_conformance_test.go` - 8 conformance\n  tests for pagination behavior validation\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/test/pagination.test.ts` -\n  TypeScript iterator tests (multi-page, single-page, error)\n- `specs/044-actual-cost-pagination/` - Feature specification,\n  plan, tasks, research, data model, contracts, and checklists\n\n- `proto/finfocus/v1/costsource.proto` - Added pagination fields\n  to `GetActualCostRequest` (page_size, page_token) and\n  `GetActualCostResponse` (next_page_token, total_count)\n- `sdk/go/proto/finfocus/v1/costsource.pb.go` - Regenerated\n  protobuf bindings\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers.go` - Added `PaginateActualCosts()`,\n  `WithNextPageToken()`, and `WithTotalCount()` functions\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers_test.go` - Added pagination unit\n  tests (default size, custom size, last page, invalid token,\n  offset beyond range, max clamping, total count, full iteration,\n  benchmark)\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/logging.go` - Added `FieldResultCount`\n  structured logging constant\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/README.md` - Added pagination documentation\n  sections\n- `sdk/go/testing/mock_plugin.go` - Added pagination support to\n  mock `GetActualCost` handler\n- `sdk/go/testing/integration_test.go` - Added paginated\n  GetActualCost integration and backward compatibility tests\n- `sdk/go/testing/benchmark_test.go` - Added pagination\n  benchmarks (single page + full iteration)\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/generated/finfocus/v1/costsource_pb.ts` -\n  Regenerated TypeScript bindings\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/utils/pagination.ts` -\n  Added `actualCostIterator()` async generator\n\nCloses #353\n\n* feat(proto): add pagination support to actual cost retrieval\n\n- Enables hosts to retrieve large cost datasets (10,000+ records)\n  in manageable pages via offset-based pagination tokens\n- Adds `page_size`/`page_token` request fields and\n  `next_page_token`/`total_count` response fields to the proto\n- Provides server-side `PaginateActualCosts()` helper in Go SDK\n  and client-side `ActualCostIterator` for transparent page\n  iteration in both Go and TypeScript\n- Maintains full backward compatibility: existing plugins and hosts\n  work unchanged when pagination fields are absent\n- Includes 8 conformance tests validating distinct pagination\n  behaviors and performance benchmarks (<100ms p99 per page)\n\n- [x] `make test` passes (all Go packages)\n- [x] `golangci-lint run ./...` passes with 0 issues\n- [x] TypeScript client build passes (`tsup` + `tsc --noEmit`)\n- [x] TypeScript tests pass (56/56 including 5 pagination tests)\n- [x] `BenchmarkPaginateActualCosts`: 112 ns/op, 2 allocs/op\n- [x] `BenchmarkGetActualCostPaginated/FullIteration`: ~5ms for\n  10K records (SC-002 target: <10s)\n- [x] 8 pagination conformance tests pass\n- [x] Backward compatibility tests pass (legacy plugin/host)\n- [x] All 51 implementation tasks verified complete\n\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/actual_cost_iterator.go` - Go client-side\n  page iterator for `GetActualCost` responses\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/actual_cost_iterator_test.go` - Iterator\n  unit tests (multi-page, single-page, error, empty, context)\n- `sdk/go/testing/pagination_conformance_test.go` - 8 conformance\n  tests for pagination behavior validation\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/test/pagination.test.ts` -\n  TypeScript iterator tests (multi-page, single-page, error)\n- `specs/044-actual-cost-pagination/` - Feature specification,\n  plan, tasks, research, data model, contracts, and checklists\n\n- `proto/finfocus/v1/costsource.proto` - Added pagination fields\n  to `GetActualCostRequest` (page_size, page_token) and\n  `GetActualCostResponse` (next_page_token, total_count)\n- `sdk/go/proto/finfocus/v1/costsource.pb.go` - Regenerated\n  protobuf bindings\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers.go` - Added `PaginateActualCosts()`,\n  `WithNextPageToken()`, and `WithTotalCount()` functions\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers_test.go` - Added pagination unit\n  tests (default size, custom size, last page, invalid token,\n  offset beyond range, max clamping, total count, full iteration,\n  benchmark)\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/logging.go` - Added `FieldResultCount`\n  structured logging constant\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/README.md` - Added pagination documentation\n  sections\n- `sdk/go/testing/mock_plugin.go` - Added pagination support to\n  mock `GetActualCost` handler\n- `sdk/go/testing/integration_test.go` - Added paginated\n  GetActualCost integration and backward compatibility tests\n- `sdk/go/testing/benchmark_test.go` - Added pagination\n  benchmarks (single page + full iteration)\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/generated/finfocus/v1/costsource_pb.ts` -\n  Regenerated TypeScript bindings\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/utils/pagination.ts` -\n  Added `actualCostIterator()` async generator\n\nCloses #353",
