          "distinct": true,
          "id": "60082d843e2fb4d4b9dd7d729daadc561c10d32c",
          "message": "fix(pluginsdk): harden pagination edge cases and observability (#376)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add `math.MaxInt32` upper bound check in `DecodePageToken` to\n  reject offsets that would overflow the int32 `total_count` field\n  in proto responses\n- Add defensive null response guards in TypeScript `actualCostIterator`\n  and `recommendationsIterator` for non-Connect-RPC transports\n- Add zerolog warnings when `page_size` exceeds `MaxPageSize` in both\n  `PaginateActualCosts` and `PaginateRecommendations`, matching the\n  existing `total_count` clamping log pattern\n- Add edge case tests for inconsistent `total_count` across pages,\n  `math.MaxInt32` boundary values, and concurrent access documentation\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `go test -race ./sdk/go/pluginsdk/...` passes\n- [x] `go test ./sdk/go/testing/...` passes\n- [x] `make test` passes across all packages\n- [x] TypeScript client builds successfully\n- [x] All 63 TypeScript tests pass (including 2 new null guard tests)\n- [x] `golangci-lint --new-from-rev=main` reports zero issues\n- [x] Pre-existing lint issues confirmed unrelated to changes\n\n## Changes\n\n### Modified files\n\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers.go` — DecodePageToken upper bound\n  check, zerolog warnings on page_size clamping\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/helpers_test.go` — TestDecodePageToken_ErrorCases\n  with 6 subtests, TestDecodePageToken_MaxInt32Succeeds, b64encode\n  helper\n- `sdk/go/pluginsdk/actual_cost_iterator_test.go` — Three new tests:\n  inconsistent total_count, int32 boundary, concurrent access doc\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/utils/pagination.ts` — Null\n  response guards in both iterator functions\n- `sdk/typescript/packages/client/test/pagination.test.ts` — Two\n  new tests for null response body handling\n\nCloses #364\nCloses #367\nCloses #368\nCloses #369",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-12T06:10:12-06:00",
